Fedora-only fix-up, kept here on purpose (the config is shared with non-Fedora builds): drop the
CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD override from configs/surface-6.18.config, as linux-surface
did for 6.19 in 4c136ec ("configs: Remove CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD override").
kernel-ark 6.18.56's Fedora configs already set CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD=m and
CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD_PCI=m on x86 and aarch64, so the x86_64 kernel is unchanged;
the override (applied to every architecture and variant) made kernel-ark's config
check (dist-configs-check) fail elsewhere, through the PM_DEVFREQ, NLS and UFS
options it pulls in.
---
diff --git a/configs/surface-6.18.config b/configs/surface-6.18.config
index 6441f1b..1c11f9c 100644
--- a/configs/surface-6.18.config
+++ b/configs/surface-6.18.config
@@ -69,12 +69,6 @@ CONFIG_VIDEO_OV8865=m
 ##
 CONFIG_APDS9960=m
 
-##
-## Build-in UFS support (required for some Surface Go devices)
-##
-CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD=m
-CONFIG_SCSI_UFSHCD_PCI=m
-
 ##
 ## Other Drivers
 ##
